    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d30-a15">

                <pb facs="0609" n="599" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv07/pg599"/>

                <head>Appendix I to HD–25</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-07-31">July 31, 1919</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">General Duval, President of the Commission on Aerial
                    Clauses.</p>
                <p rendition="#flush">To the President of the Supreme Council of the Peace
                    Conference.</p>
                <p>I have the honour to submit herewith the report addressed to General Groves by
                    the British Military Mission at Berlin.</p>
                <p>General Groves, British Delegate of the Commission on Aerial Clauses has asked me
                    to draw the attention of the Supreme Council to this report so that instructions
                    may be given to the Commander-in-Chief to oppose the sale of the motors in
                    question.</p>
                <p>This report clearly shows the importance of the facts mentioned and I think it is
                    necessary that this question should be examined without delay.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Duval</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
